WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.200
- We have time for just
one more feel good story.

00:00:02.200 --> 00:00:03.033
And it's a good one, y'all.

00:00:03.033 --> 00:00:04.459
This is "What I'm Liking".

00:00:04.459 --> 00:00:05.639
(upbeat tempo)

00:00:05.639 --> 00:00:07.730
(audience cheering)

00:00:07.730 --> 00:00:10.130
So this one comes from our
neighbors to the north.

00:00:10.130 --> 00:00:11.970
Last year, 14 year old Anthony moved

00:00:11.970 --> 00:00:13.810
to a new neighborhood in Edmonton.

00:00:13.810 --> 00:00:15.100
His family is from Africa

00:00:15.100 --> 00:00:17.460
and his dream is to play for the NBA.

00:00:17.460 --> 00:00:20.950
So every day he practiced
for hours in his driveway,

00:00:20.950 --> 00:00:22.710
even though he had no net.

00:00:22.710 --> 00:00:24.630
Anthony was worried the constant dribbling

00:00:24.630 --> 00:00:26.700
bothered his neighbors and sure enough,

00:00:26.700 --> 00:00:29.140
one of them eventually confronted him.

00:00:29.140 --> 00:00:31.460
But take a look here.
This was a good thing.

00:00:31.460 --> 00:00:35.050
The neighborhood came together
and bought Anthony a hoop.

00:00:35.050 --> 00:00:36.806
It was such a sweet gesture.

00:00:36.806 --> 00:00:37.639
(audience claps)

00:00:37.639 --> 00:00:40.890
Many people noticed,
including LeBron James.

00:00:40.890 --> 00:00:43.160
Let's get Anthony and his
neighbor, Ian, in here.

00:00:43.160 --> 00:00:45.594
They watch on City TV at five PM.

00:00:45.594 --> 00:00:46.427
(audience cheering)

00:00:46.427 --> 00:00:50.540
What's up y'all?

00:00:50.540 --> 00:00:52.180
All right. So Ian, I'm
going to start with you.

00:00:52.180 --> 00:00:55.160
You organize this. So
how did it come about?

00:00:55.160 --> 00:00:58.720
- Yeah, I just noticed this
kid that was constantly

00:00:58.720 --> 00:01:01.264
dribbling his ball up and down the block.

00:01:01.264 --> 00:01:05.443
Just being a good kid, playing
on his driveway, dribbling.

00:01:06.736 --> 00:01:08.810
And I thought, hey,
let's get this kid a net.

00:01:08.810 --> 00:01:10.610
I noticed he didn't
have a hoop to shoot on.

00:01:10.610 --> 00:01:15.610
So yeah, I just created a post
on a Facebook community page

00:01:16.480 --> 00:01:17.763
here on the north side.

00:01:19.710 --> 00:01:23.440
We were just overwhelmed
with all the support of God

00:01:23.440 --> 00:01:25.990
and everyone wanting to help this kid out.

00:01:25.990 --> 00:01:28.900
- Oh my gosh, I love your
Canadian accent right now, man.

00:01:28.900 --> 00:01:30.730
I'm so in love with you. (laughs)

00:01:30.730 --> 00:01:31.563
(audience laughs)

00:01:31.563 --> 00:01:33.170
And you look like a lumberjack,
this is just like my dream.

00:01:33.170 --> 00:01:34.272
This is awesome.

00:01:34.272 --> 00:01:35.105
(audience cheers)

00:01:35.105 --> 00:01:35.938
It's so awesome.

00:01:37.384 --> 00:01:41.570
So Anthony, so LeBron
James saw what happened.

00:01:41.570 --> 00:01:44.710
That's super cool, but he's
not the only one, right?

00:01:44.710 --> 00:01:46.753
- Yeah. That's true, Ms. Clarkson.

00:01:48.976 --> 00:01:50.213
When LeBron James saw that,

00:01:50.213 --> 00:01:51.910
that just completely blew my mind.

00:01:51.910 --> 00:01:54.810
Like I wanted to pass out on
the spot right there and like,

00:01:54.810 --> 00:01:55.890
yeah, that's it right there.

00:01:55.890 --> 00:01:58.010
So like, it was just like,

00:01:58.010 --> 00:02:00.900
it was kind of insane because
LeBron is like my idol.

00:02:00.900 --> 00:02:03.600
He's the person who I've
always looked up to.

00:02:03.600 --> 00:02:05.170
And like many people reach out

00:02:05.170 --> 00:02:07.750
to like people here at Northside

00:02:07.750 --> 00:02:10.310
people kept re-posting it on Twitter.

00:02:10.310 --> 00:02:11.360
It was on TSN.

00:02:11.360 --> 00:02:14.010
And then when it was on
TSN, I was sweating buckets.

00:02:14.010 --> 00:02:14.843
And like,

00:02:14.843 --> 00:02:15.676
- Aww.

00:02:15.676 --> 00:02:16.509
- It just made me feel good knowing

00:02:16.509 --> 00:02:20.380
everybody here has my back
and to making it to the NBA.

00:02:20.380 --> 00:02:22.959
Because that's my goal, to
make it to the NBA. It's funny.

00:02:22.959 --> 00:02:23.824
(audience cheers)

00:02:23.824 --> 00:02:26.310
- That's amazing, and
it's an amazing goal.

00:02:26.310 --> 00:02:28.450
Thank you so much, Ian.

00:02:28.450 --> 00:02:29.550
And thank you, Anthony,

00:02:29.550 --> 00:02:31.630
and good luck getting into the NBA, man.

00:02:31.630 --> 00:02:33.660
I'm liking your post right now.

00:02:33.660 --> 00:02:36.810
(audience cheers)

00:02:36.810 --> 00:02:37.810
Absolutely.

00:02:37.810 --> 00:02:38.890
I'm going to have you back on

00:02:38.890 --> 00:02:40.700
when you're playing for the NBA.

00:02:40.700 --> 00:02:41.750
That's not all, though.

00:02:41.750 --> 00:02:43.160
Our season long partner Pilot Pin,

00:02:43.160 --> 00:02:44.670
the go-to pin of the Kelly Clarkson Show,

00:02:44.670 --> 00:02:47.200
thinks that this story is
as sweet and cool as we do.

00:02:47.200 --> 00:02:49.130
So Anthony, in recognition,

00:02:49.130 --> 00:02:51.450
they'd like to write you a
check for a thousand dollars

00:02:51.450 --> 00:02:52.780
to help you get on your way.

00:02:52.780 --> 00:02:54.146
(audience cheers)

00:02:54.146 --> 00:02:54.979
(Kelly laughs)

00:02:54.979 --> 00:02:55.812
- What?

00:02:56.990 --> 00:02:58.840
- Oh my God, I love it, I love it.

00:02:58.840 --> 00:02:59.840
- Thank you so much.

